what is a DOM?
Imagine a Web Page is Like Your Bedroom 
YOUR BEDROOM (Web Page)
┌─────────────────────────────────┐
│  📚 Bookshelf (with books)      │
│  🛏️ Bed (with pillows, sheets)  │
│  💻 Desk (laptop, lamp, notes)  │
│  🚪 Door                        │
│  🪟 Window                       │
└─────────────────────────────────┘
->DOM = Your actual bedroom after you arrange everything 🏠
You can MOVE furniture
You can PAINT walls
You can ADD/REMOVE items
Everything is ALIVE and CHANGEABLE
->DOM = Interactive Toy Room
TOY ROOM (DOM)
├── 🏗️ Building Blocks (Elements: <div>, <p>)
├── 📝 Sticky Notes (Text: "Hello World")  
├── 🗣️ Whisper Notes (Comments: <!-- secret -->)
├── 📦 Storage Box (DocumentFragment)
└── 📋 Room Blueprint (Document)
->Browser Builds a FAMILY TREE in Memory
          DOCUMENT (Grandparent) -> 9
              |
           <html> (Parent) -> 1
           /     \
     <head>     <body> (Children) ->1
       |          /  \
  <title>      <h1>  <p> (Grandchildren) ->1
     |           |     |
  "My Page"   "Hello" "Welcome!" (Great-grandchildren) ->3
Each item in the tree = "NODE" (family member)
->DOM in One Picture
          YOU (JavaScript)
             ↓
         "Hey DOM!"
             ↓
       ┌─────────────────┐
       │  DOM (Tree)     │
       │  ├── Document   │ ← The Boss 👑
       │  ├── Elements   │ ← The Soldiers 🪖  
       │  ├── Text       │ ← The Messengers 📨
       │  ├── Comments   │ ← The Secrets 🤫
       │  └── Fragment   │ ← The Magic Box 🎁
       └─────────────────┘
             ↓
    Browser paints on SCREEN 🖥️
             ↓
      You SEE the changes 👀
all node type
NODE TYPE HIERARCHY:
EventTarget (Root)
    ↓
   Node (All nodes inherit from here)
    ├── Document (9) ──────┐
    │   ├── DocumentType (10)  // <!DOCTYPE>
    │   └── Element (1) <html> │
    │       ├── Element (1) <head>   // HTML Elements
    │       │   └── Element (1) <title>
    │       │       └── Text (3) "Page Title"
    │       └── Element (1) <body>   // HTML Elements
    │           ├── Comment (8) <!-- note -->
    │           ├── Element (1) <div>
    │           │   └── Text (3) "Content"
    │           └── Element (1) <script>
    │
    ├── DocumentFragment (11)  // Lightweight container
    ├── Element (1)            // HTML/SVG/MathML elements
    ├── Text (3)               // Text content
    ├── Comment (8)            // <!-- comments -->
    ├── CDATASection (4)       // <![CDATA[ ]]>
    ├── ProcessingInstruction (7) // <?xml ?>
    ├── Attribute (2)          // Deprecated
    ├── EntityReference (5)    // Deprecated
    ├── Entity (6)             // Deprecated
    └── Notation (12)          // Deprecated
Nodes tree daily used node:
1 = ELEMENT    → 🏗️  Building blocks (has tagName)
3 = TEXT       → 📝  Content (has nodeValue)
8 = COMMENT    → 💬  Notes (has nodeValue)
9 = DOCUMENT   → 👑  Root (special methods)
11 = FRAGMENT  → 📦  Temporary box

Remember: 1+3=4 (Element+Text=basic content)
          9+11=20 (Document+Fragment=DOM magic)

When to Use What:
Need to show something? → Element (1) + Text (3)
Need to hide notes? → Comment (8)
Need to batch updates? → DocumentFragment (11)
Need to access page? → Document (9)


// QUIZ: What are the node types?
const div = document.createElement('div');
div.innerHTML = 'Hello <!-- comment --> World';

// Answer:
// div.nodeType = 1 (ELEMENT)
// div.childNodes[0].nodeType = 3 (TEXT) "Hello "
// div.childNodes[1].nodeType = 8 (COMMENT) " comment "
// div.childNodes[2].nodeType = 3 (TEXT) " World"
